# Sample 10 — Advisory (should) vs mandatory (must)
#
# `must` sets the mandatory bounds an engineer refuses to cross;
# `should` sets a more conservative PREFERRED bound inside them,
# without narrowing what is compliant. Here the mandatory floor is
# 4 kA (must), but 5 kA (should) is preferred. A 4.5 kA setting is
# compliant (inside mandatory) yet CAUTION (outside preferred) —
# purely because of the advisory criterion, with no margin involved.

diagram "Advisory limit" {
  orientation horizontal
  scale linear
  range auto

  below "Absolute minimum (hard limit)" must 4 kA
  below "Preferred minimum (advisory)" should 5 kA
  above "Fault clearance" must 9 kA margin 10%

  selected "Setting" 4.5 kA
}
